<title>USA: ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF FREDRIK NYBERG.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-PROFILE OF FREDRIK NYBERG.</headline>
<dateline>BRECKENRIDGE, Colorado 1996-11-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a</p>
<p>brief profile of Fredrik Nyberg, winner of the men's World Cup</p>
<p>giant slalom in Breckenridge, Colorado, on Saturday:</p>
<p>Age: 27</p>
<p>Nationality: Sweden</p>
<p>Previous World Cup victories (4, all giant slalom) -</p>
<p>Veysonnaz Switzerland, 1990; Mt. Hutt, New Zealand, 1990;</p>
<p>Kranjska Gora, Slovenia, 1994; Aspen, U.S., 1994.</p>
<p>Other: At 72 kg Nyberg is among the smallest first-seed</p>
<p>racers. &quot;I used to be even smaller, but strength isn't all</p>
<p>there is to racing. You also must have feel for the snow.&quot;</p>
</text>
